persistcalls_x86_64 -- the GH-1034 call-guard fixture for option `persistcalls`
(tests/stages/kuna-persistcalls.xml).

What it is
  A 33,624-byte x86-64 ELF built from persistcalls_x86_64.c, which is generated
  straight-line C. `churn` reads, then writes, each of 256 writable globals in
  .data, with a call to `sink` after every write and one more inside a branch
  every eighth step (288 calls). `sink` clobbers memory, so every global is read
  again after the calls before it. `small` touches two globals across three
  calls, the control far below the option's threshold.

Why it is vendored
  The op counts the stage test pins depend on the exact code layout, so the
  binary is checked in rather than built at test time (CI's gcc 15 would lay the
  functions out differently).

Where it came from
  gcc 11.4.0 (Ubuntu 11.4.0-1ubuntu1~22.04.3), GNU ld 2.38, x86-64 Linux:

      gcc -O2 -fno-pie -no-pie -fno-inline -o persistcalls_x86_64 persistcalls_x86_64.c

  sha256 6d496384e809c2d6ba14303f6731ecce89082f9d74f3dd2854e6ece947d0c6d5.
  Run with no arguments it prints 23817576453 67 23817685162 76.
